From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:32:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tlc): sharper-edge and offset models for the picked-spot
 edge correction

The picked-spot fit was a parabola in ln g: measured position = true * g(x).
Real plates can have edge effects confined to the outer lanes, and an additive
part (late solvent entry) that a height-proportional model cannot fix.

- Model: measured Rf = true Rf * (1 + s(u)) + b(u), polynomials in lateral
  position u. Candidates: parabola, sharper edges (degree 4), each with or
  without an offset. Offset needs compounds at clearly different heights.
- Complexity chosen by leave-one-out cross-validation and raised only when it
  predicts left-out spots >10 % better, so few picks fall back to the parabola.
- New gates: F test of the curve against no curve, SNR 1.5x scatter.
  Simulated: flat plates are 'corrected' in 0.5 % of cases, 2-6 % curves with
  1-2 % noise are found in >99 %.
- Corrected Rf = (Rf - offset) / gain; offset exported as edge_offset, drawn
  in the straightened preview, model name shown in the panel.

